  "notes": "Scotts Miracle-Gro Co (NYSE: SMG). Largest US consumer lawn & garden brand (Scotts, Miracle-Gro, Roundup distribution agreement) plus Hawthorne Gardening (indoor / hydroponics, Gen 1 cannabis-cultivation supplier). Fiscal year ends last Saturday of September. Data from SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts (CIK 0000825542). EBITDA = operating income + D&A. Net debt = LongTermDebtNoncurrent + LongTermDebtCurrent \u2212 cash. FY21 was peak (COVID gardening boom + Hawthorne hydroponics demand pull from cannabis legalization wave); FY22-24 collapse driven by post-COVID consumer rollback PLUS Hawthorne cannabis-segment crash (revenue fell from $1.4B FY21 to <$300M by FY24, multi-billion goodwill writedowns). Heavy debt-paydown campaign FY23-25; FY25 profitability returning to core US Consumer.",
